Aapka folder structure dekh kar samajh aa raha hai ki aapne **Django** ka project setup kar liya hai. Aapke main project ka naam `snake` hai aur aapne ek app banayi hai jiska naam `kobra` hai.

Django mein ek browser-based Snake Game banane ke liye humein game ka logic (HTML/JavaScript) likhna hoga aur use Django views ke through serve karna hoga. Yahan step-by-step process hai:

### Step 1: App ko Settings mein add karein

Sabse pehle `snake/settings.py` file open karein aur `INSTALLED_APPS` list mein apni `kobra` app ko add karein.

```python
INSTALLED_APPS = [
    'django.contrib.admin',
    'django.contrib.auth',
    'django.contrib.contenttypes',
    'django.contrib.sessions',
    'django.contrib.messages',
    'django.contrib.staticfiles',
    'kobra', # Yahan apni app add karein
]

```

### Step 2: Templates Folder Banayein

Django ko HTML file dikhane ke liye templates folder ki zaroorat hoti hai.

1. Apne `kobra` folder ke andar ek naya folder banayein jiska naam **`templates`** ho.
2. Us `templates` folder ke andar ek aur folder banayein jiska naam **`kobra`** ho (Django standards ke mutabiq).
3. Ab iske andar apni HTML file banayein: `index.html`.
*(Final path: `kobra/templates/kobra/index.html`)*

### Step 3: Game ka Code Likhna (`index.html`)

Ab us `index.html` file ko open karein aur usme HTML5 Canvas aur JavaScript ka ye basic Snake Game code paste karein:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Snake Game</title>
    <style>
        body {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            background-color: #222;
            color: white;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            flex-direction: column;
        }
        canvas {
            background-color: black;
            border: 2px solid #4CAF50;
            box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.5);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h2>Python(Kobra) Snake Game 🐍</h2>
    <canvas id="gameCanvas" width="400" height="400"></canvas>

    <script>
        const canvas = document.getElementById("gameCanvas");
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");

        let gridSize = 20;
        let snake = [{x: 200, y: 200}];
        let food = {x: 100, y: 100};
        let dx = 0;
        let dy = -gridSize;
        let score = 0;

        function drawGame() {
            // Screen clear karein
            ctx.fillStyle = "black";
            ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

            // Food draw karein
            ctx.fillStyle = "red";
            ctx.fillRect(food.x, food.y, gridSize, gridSize);

            // Snake move karein
            let head = {x: snake[0].x + dx, y: snake[0].y + dy};
            snake.unshift(head);

            // Khana khaya ya nahi?
            if (head.x === food.x && head.y === food.y) {
                score++;
                spawnFood();
            } else {
                snake.pop(); // Khana nahi khaya to tail hatao
            }

            // Snake draw karein
            ctx.fillStyle = "lime";
            snake.forEach(segment => ctx.fillRect(segment.x, segment.y, gridSize, gridSize));

            // Game Over logic
            if (head.x < 0 || head.x >= canvas.width || head.y < 0 || head.y >= canvas.height || collision(head)) {
                alert("Game Over! Score: " + score);
                snake = [{x: 200, y: 200}];
                dx = 0; dy = -gridSize;
                score = 0;
            }
        }

        function collision(head) {
            for(let i = 1; i < snake.length; i++) {
                if(head.x === snake[i].x && head.y === snake[i].y) return true;
            }
            return false;
        }

        function spawnFood() {
            food.x = Math.floor(Math.random() * (canvas.width / gridSize)) * gridSize;
            food.y = Math.floor(Math.random() * (canvas.height / gridSize)) * gridSize;
        }

        document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
            if (e.key === "ArrowUp" && dy === 0) { dx = 0; dy = -gridSize; }
            if (e.key === "ArrowDown" && dy === 0) { dx = 0; dy = gridSize; }
            if (e.key === "ArrowLeft" && dx === 0) { dx = -gridSize; dy = 0; }
            if (e.key === "ArrowRight" && dx === 0) { dx = gridSize; dy = 0; }
        });

        setInterval(drawGame, 100);
    </script>
</body>
</html>

```

### Step 4: View Banayein (`kobra/views.py`)

Is HTML page ko render karne ke liye `kobra/views.py` mein ek function banayein:

```python
from django.shortcuts import render

def game_view(request):
    return render(request, 'kobra/index.html')

```

### Step 5: URLs Connect Karein (`snake/urls.py`)

Ab project ki main urls file (`snake/urls.py`) ko open karein aur apne view ka rasta (path) set karein:

```python
from django.contrib import admin
from django.urls import path
from kobra import views  # Apni app ke views import karein

urlpatterns = [
    path('admin/', admin.site.urls),
    path('', views.game_view, name='game'), # Root url par game chalega
]

```

### Step 6: Server Run Karein

Terminal/Command Prompt open karein, wahan jayen jahan `manage.py` rakhi hai, aur command likhein:

```bash
python manage.py runserver

```

Browser open karein aur `[http://127.0.0.1:8000/](http://127.0.0.1:8000/)` par jayein. Aapka Snake Game wahan chal raha hoga! Keyboard ki arrow keys se aap snake ko control kar sakte hain.